course: dictionary
lesson: 7102
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word peak is a good example. It can mean a mountain top, the highest point of something, or the busiest time. The words around it give the clue.
explain: «Mount Everest has the highest peak above sea level, 8,849 metres.» Mountains, height and metres show that peak means the pointed top of a mountain. In a graph, the words highest value point to a different meaning: the top point of a line on a chart.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Trains are dearer at peak times» makes sense if peak means the busiest times, because crowded trains often cost more. Peak can also be a verb: «The Geminids, peaking around 13 to 14 December» means they reach their highest point then.
fact: Peak can mean the pointed top of a mountain, or the highest point or level of something.
fact: To peak means to reach the highest point, as in «The Geminids, peaking around 13 to 14 December».
fact: Peak can also mean the busiest or best time, as in peak hours. Off-peak times are usually cheaper.
fact: The peak of a cap is the stiff part that sticks out at the front.
fact: «Mount Everest» has the highest peak above sea level, at 8,849 metres.
exercise: «Mount Everest has the highest peak above sea level, 8,849 metres.» What does peak mean in this sentence? | To get busy | A cheap train ticket | *The pointed top of a mountain | The stiff front of a cap
exercise: «Trains are dearer at peak times.» What are peak times? | The quietest times, when trains are empty | The times just after midnight | *The busiest times | The times when the weather is best
exercise: «The Geminids, peaking around 13 to 14 December, are one of the richest showers of the year.» What does peaking mean here? | Stopping for a rest | *Reaching the highest point | Hiding from view | Going down slowly
test: «The peak of the line graph is its highest value.» What does peak mean in this sentence? | A kind of hat | *The highest point or level | The start of the line | A bridge over the water
test: «That's peak,» mutters Harrison, after his brothers break his controller. In London slang, what does peak mean here? | Brother or mate | Very fast | *Bad luck or annoying | Fine and good
exam: «Everest put inside the Challenger Deep would have its peak about 2 km under water.» What does peak mean here? | The bottom of the sea floor | The deepest point of the sea | *The highest point of the mountain | A shop that sells tickets
